-- divisibility club

Theorem.

  a. 3 divides 12.
  b. 1 divides every integer.
  c. Every integer divides itself.
  d. Any integer divides 0.

-- congruences in action

Theorem.  Let a, b, c, d, m : ℤ.

  a. a ≡ a (mod m).
  b. If a ≡ b (mod m) then b ≡ a (mod m).
  c. If a ≡ b (mod m) and b ≡ c (mod m) then a ≡ c (mod m).
